{"title":"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(A_Little_Bashy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (A Little Bashy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Very_algebraic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Very algebraic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee730ecd30681b47e111b69adcc41031307559c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a : b : c : d=1 : 2 : 3 : 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e844b013cb07a4ccd130fcea1b7ab985ba0b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, what is the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be a number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/2477bca83e751716a47abc0c320ea79c21f631b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a \\mid 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cbab3f9c79e043adff2da9920bd7540d1b398884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a \\mid 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2d39cffc92a7af2288969ede42fc754c8a2b13e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a \\mid 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5289b707425ca0256235693b55909e94396b19b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12a \\mid 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. This implies the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/94758278560625599bb94834f1452e69e1a0b015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252/12 = \\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"110\" height=\"25\" />, which works.\n</p><p>~Bradygho\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/95500b1de5ebb1421ffcf1d0ed30fd9986e7c711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252=2^2\\cdot 3^2\\cdot 7$\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a0874c15e47cf556c14c7f59e27992d91c3aacec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7eb70570d9064899e204827b67610706dedc65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=4a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> it is invalid for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. With similar reasoning, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must have at most one factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a19307f3333bfa4ca37ff87921b5e00cf4e3fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"65\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d2025bb35622bbd802d3d4eef27cc9dbd59be4b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c70e8c01ca7e2ae55bfec1cba9ca7883b41622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=42, c=63, d=84,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" /> which is valid)\n</p><p>~Apple321\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28A_Little_Bashy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(A_Little_Bashy)\">Solution 3 (A Little Bashy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (A Little Bashy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b194959074d0755697f60356a3095000d2a70a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252=2^2 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />, so the divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c597899d3d95b48fa2bc940b53f74db78e9d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4,6,7,9,12,14,18,21,28,36,42,63,84,126,252 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"439\" height=\"20\" />. We see the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde5637d85cd84f49c939e8382358ad2e00df870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{21,42,63,84 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" /> is the largest 4-digit set we can form, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a19307f3333bfa4ca37ff87921b5e00cf4e3fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\boxed{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"65\" height=\"25\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f40b1e5cfdb4e4b37d0f5d1c57a5c893020e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\linebreak$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"22\" />\n~Geometry285\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Very_algebraic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Very_algebraic)\">Solution 4 (Very algebraic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Very algebraic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b1015c504b8fa66637dfb9c5565b1d43080ab9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1cb96a3344461b85f9e6eb91850987abd720a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4666d5b88a5a12f9055189db2a68e4135c67f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> must also divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc50bdf94a6d964577583bb49a7e556dccd428e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c6d12fe80f8e9cad3e74c9f8cce1fc1b61a26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{252}{3a},\\frac{252}{4a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" /> are both integers, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> divides and multiplying, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4131457f67c5dbfd8b1c6be1f74a47595a9bd3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f02cdb77e00acfa947ee95374de5ceef6cb57d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> The greatest common divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4131457f67c5dbfd8b1c6be1f74a47595a9bd3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/848ec5b5f695afbacb864efead154761481780c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/f/0ef9ca64d92c34ac479e415fd7a4a0bf81d19028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> and we can check that indeed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb04820e88558ecce603bce1d37e8c145aaab05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\boxed{21}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"70\" height=\"25\" /> ~samrocksnature\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015816\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 235/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7559/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.232      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    5.232      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21591:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015816 and revision id 270880. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}